<title>PERU: Peru net reserves rise to $8.448 bln on Sept 4.</title>
<headline>Peru net reserves rise to $8.448 bln on Sept 4.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Central Reserve Bank said Monday its net international reserves stood at $8.448 billion on September 4, up from $8.349 billion the week before.</p>
<p>The bank's foreign exchange position, or total liquidity minus short- and long-term debt obligations, was $1.731 billion on September 4.</p>
<p>International reserves ended 1995 at $6.641 billion.</p>
<p>-- Saul Hudson, Lima Newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
